# Copy to .env to point the app at a LOCAL test backend.
#
# Leave this unset (or delete .env) and the app runs fully offline on sample
# data — that is the default, and it is not an error state.
#
# The app REFUSES any host that could be production. Accepted:
#   - localhost / 127.0.0.1
#   - a private LAN address (10.x, 192.168.x, 172.16–31.x) — how Expo Go on a
#     phone reaches a laptop on the same wifi
#   - a .local hostname
#   - a hostname starting with test. / dev. / staging.
# Anything else fails at startup with an explanation. See src/api/config.ts.
#
# Run the backend from Calder35/youdecide-ai-backend:
#   uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
#
# NOTE: the seller-intake routes this app calls (/v1/users, /v1/journeys, …)
# live on the backend's `feat/01-data-model` branch, not on its `main`.

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
